From 9d52b84363a8dd2b02d17d419241d8838ea8e313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:11:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] [B70][XPU] Native per-token int8 act quant + oneDNN int8
 W8A8 GEMM

_C::dynamic_per_token_scaled_int8_quant: one work-group per token row,
absmax reduce then quantize, bit-exact mirror of vLLM's
xpu_ops.dynamic_per_token_int8_quant_ref (scale rounded to the input
dtype, round-half-even, precise fp under icpx fast-math).

_xpu_C::int8_scaled_mm: port of vllm-xpu-kernels#196 narrowed to the
symmetric Int8ScaledMM path (s8 x s8 -> f16/bf16, per-token or
per-tensor A scale, per-channel or per-tensor B scale, bias). Per-token
scale as a oneDNN src-scale attribute (groups {1,K}); falls back to a
binary_mul post-op (bias moved behind it) when oneDNN reports it
unimplemented, or with B70_INT8_GEMM_SCALE_MODE=postop.
